  "details": "The way the moderation for groups works right now is horrible. I feel like with how much the live now tab has been pushed, the groups fair, the pride hub events, etc. there needs to be more care put into how moderators and moderation tools are implemented. \n\nFor example; why is there no search function under the banned users on the website? A group I moderate has around 1,200 members banned. There is no order to the bans on the website and it takes a third party software to unban someone if banned incorrectly. \n\nAlongside that, I would love to be able to kick someone without it doing anything to their trust rank. Sometimes we have people fall asleep in our instances, so we kick them when we close the instance for their safety. I would also like to be able to kick/ban/warn someone with a reason that shows them why they were moderated, which rule they broke, and how long it will be before they can join back if they were kicked. \n\nI heard there is a moderation overhaul in the works, and i really hope some of these simply quality of life things are implemented. i don't want to have to use third party software for moderation.",
